# Floe — Controls

This file fixes the keys the game answers to and what each one drives. What each
screen does with an action is in `specs/ui.md`, and the hop cadence a held
direction repeats at is in `specs/hopping.md`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
## How input reaches the game

This game stands on no engine, so the keyboard belongs to the runtime layer you
write. The game is driven by physical keys, read as `KeyboardEvent.code` values
so a binding is the same key on every layout.

| Key | Drives |
| --- | --- |
| `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` | Up |
| `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` | Down |
| `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` | Left |
| `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` | Right |
| `Enter`, `Space` | Confirm |
| `Escape` | Back |
| `KeyP`, `Escape` | Pause |
| `KeyM` | Mute |
| `Backquote` | The debug overlay |

The game answers to these keys and to no others.
{{else}}
## How input reaches the game

The {{engine.name}} engine owns the keyboard and documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. The game registers named actions with
it and reads them back; it never reads a key event itself.

`LAYOUT` is the control scheme the engine is built with, `ACTIONS` is the whole
vocabulary the game registers, and `BINDINGS` maps each action to the
`KeyboardEvent.code` values that fire it.

| Action | Keys |
| --- | --- |
| `up` | `ArrowUp`, `KeyW` |
| `down` | `ArrowDown`, `KeyS` |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft`, `KeyA` |
| `right` | `ArrowRight`, `KeyD` |
| `confirm` | `Enter`, `Space` |
| `back` | `Escape` |
| `pause` | `KeyP`, `Escape` |
| `mute` | `KeyM` |

The game registers these eight actions and no others.
{{/if}}

## What each one does

| Action | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Up, down, left, right | On the `playing` screen, hop the critter one tile that way. On a screen with a menu, move the highlight one item that way, wrapping at both ends. |
| Confirm | Accept the highlighted menu item. |
| Back | Leave the screen in front of the player. |
| Pause | Open the pause menu from the `playing` screen. |
| Mute | Toggle sound, from any screen. |

`Escape` drives both pause and back. On the `playing` screen it pauses; on every
other screen it goes back.

## How each one is read

The four movement actions are read as held on the `playing` screen, so a held
direction hops the critter repeatedly at the cadence `specs/hopping.md` fixes. On
every other screen they are read as press edges, so one press moves the highlight
one item.

Confirm, back, pause, and mute are read as press edges everywhere, so each fires
once per press however long the key is held.

## The debug overlay

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The backtick key (`Backquote`) shows and hides the debug overlay, which is part
of the runtime layer you write. `specs/instrumentation.md` fixes what the overlay
reports.
{{else}}
The backtick key (`Backquote`) shows and hides the engine's debug overlay. The
engine handles that key itself rather than through a registered action, so it is
outside `ACTIONS`. `specs/instrumentation.md` fixes what the game registers for
the overlay to report.
{{/if}}
